{"title":"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Using_Logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Using Logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Before the district play, the Unicorns had won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/00890d0beefe80ec2a7d63ca91aaa8b8056ba355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of their basketball games. During district play, they won six more games and lost two, to finish the season having won half their games. How many games did the Unicorns play in all?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244c5f82a799eab1ff97e98506a2529e4c8b466b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 48\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 52\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 54\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the beginning of the problem, the Unicorns had played <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> games and they had won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of these games. From the information given in the problem, we can say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e8388be05801d6562f813fc6cd94b21f0be68771.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}=0.45.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"74\" height=\"36\" /> Next, the Unicorns win 6 more games and lose 2 more, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d73c3195400c13debe4c3062d29a6a1c2549b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> games played during district play. We are told that they end the season having won half of their games, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> of their games. We can write another equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a88333d8a91f799d0884b7ef4baa1d0c448a920f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+6}{y+8}=0.5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" /> This gives us a system of equations:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ceab2dfef83f6d67de18f32f9c6ee94427b7d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}=0.45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"70\" height=\"36\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a88333d8a91f799d0884b7ef4baa1d0c448a920f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+6}{y+8}=0.5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" />\nWe first multiply both sides of the first equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/162196910e27445254b6eb2fa312775f6f107731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0.45y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" /> Then, we multiply both sides of the second equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f20c09ed436f7f7425c41b31c7e84a3eb7e497c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y+8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a63005dc5da4068a28468183908533477dcf308.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+6=0.5(y+8).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" /> Applying the Distributive Property gives yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d3f7d53ef8b4cf68991472e6ae10e22d9e90f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+6=0.5y+4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" /> Now we substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/d/5bd9174b08f4a12c29a14d982019ec9718fc1ca0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.45y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/68686d21201baad71859142eb5338f6b9df0754e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.45y+6=0.5y+4.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" /> Solving gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d04d626af72c90cbbd27b712f4e3f3b080600ea4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=40.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> Since the problem asks for the total number of games, we add on the last 8 games to get the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b36470e66be9e798f9a64864745decb58c8a7bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can check each answer choice from left to right to see which one is correct. Suppose the Unicorns played <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games in total. Then, after district play, they would have won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games. Now, consider the situation before district play. The Unicorns would have won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Converting to a percentage, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3ec4f05fc174cb91c8900517458956ce4a34804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18/40 = 45\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1717aeedab5f79f259ae59a92d605e13246421bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>Note: If A didn't work, we would have similarly tested the other choices until we found one that did.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cxsmi\">cxsmi</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Using_Logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Using_Logic)\">Solution 3 (Using Logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Using Logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01df53b60e80f73d3981f9b7e04cb395597f91df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\%=\\frac9{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />. Therefore, the number of games before district play must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in order for the number of games won to be an integer. The Unicorns played <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63d73c3195400c13debe4c3062d29a6a1c2549b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> more games during district play. The only answer choice that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1717aeedab5f79f259ae59a92d605e13246421bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the start of the problem we figure out the Unicorns have won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/00890d0beefe80ec2a7d63ca91aaa8b8056ba355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of their games, which can be represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ceee43172f0ac3b724475ff9b32d6a40fdfb782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac9{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. Since this is a simplified fraction and not necessarily the amount of games they have played, we can add a variable (in this case I am using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />) to the numerator and denominator to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/1/4916076583b242e6e1a7a032e107a84466a692cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x}{20x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"34\" height=\"38\" />. We then know that during the district play they have won 6 more games and lost 2 of them for a total of 6+2=8 games played. We then can add it to our fraction we have built to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28df8dacb156e4f9f9f1918896b328ad1c08b56d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x+6}{20x+8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"66\" height=\"40\" />. We also know that the fraction is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61a6afbaf13ab37eff0443c10cf204d50f54bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Putting these equations together we get  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/5026da43b19b9c6bf855065a30d6e3285cdbb0b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x+6}{20x+8}=\\frac1{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"103\" height=\"40\" />. Now we can cross multiply to come out with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b2b5cbd225479c1d122ef7a1270a84cf4ce92f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18x+12=20x+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" />. We now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />!<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b2b5cbd225479c1d122ef7a1270a84cf4ce92f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18x+12=20x+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"15\" /> ----&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a5811f895aa94bae42b39b41b69f7c6efecc999b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> ----&gt; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587c08a7a7f6a73eb4871e10c8d0ff332dfc0812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. After we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> which comes out to be 2 we then plug it back into the denominator to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/9/049785edb48c47ba9c07e6de306902eb54137ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20(2)+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> which is equal to 48, so the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1717aeedab5f79f259ae59a92d605e13246421bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} 48}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"61\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Am24\">AM24</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=1993\">https://youtu.be/rQUwNC0gqdg?t=1993</a>\n</p><p>~pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/1CAxNXM8TWo\">https://youtu.be/1CAxNXM8TWo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 8\">2007 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2007\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" alig